        Algorithm idea: MultiMeter separates sub-meters by 1 blank column "Meter_draw" at x offsets computed as i*(subwidth+1), subwidth=(width-(subcols-1))/subcols truncated. For width48, subwidth=(48-7)/8=5, then right cells would also width5, contradiction. Unless MultiMeter's width for right meter is 55? Right column width maybe is 55 not 48 because header column allocation beyond right text start... At W100 right column span from50 to 99 (50 width if no trailing margin) and meter width 48? If right subwidth computed (55-7)/8=6. Header geometry maybe rightmost column extends to terminal edge (100) not 98, meter width for last column might be 50? Cells start50, pitch6 (width5+sep) for first 7 cells, last cell at92 width6? Last cell content " 90[0]" length6 - if its base cell width were5+sep, what's its content? label3 + [ + interior1 + ] =6 (width6!) Wait cell width definition includes label+brackets+interior. A width5 cell cannot have interior. But maybe Meter_draw for a submeter is passed width = *remaining width to end of column* not subwidth, and it internally draws bar of width maybe min(...) and returns width used? CPUMeter draw might compute its own width based on number of subcolumns parameter stored in meter (`column` count) and header width... 
        Let's postpone exact CPU packed rendering until investigating varying widths systematically after basic main works. For now use subWidth = width/subcols (floor), pitch=subWidth. For right48 =>6 correct, left47=>5 but pitch5 would pack cells without spaces giving last cells misplaced vs original (pitch6). To match positions, use pitch = (width)/(subcols) *? plus ? Use subWidth = (width - (subcols-1))/subcols if that * (??) for right gives 5 mismatch.
        Alternative pitch model: pitch = ceil(width/subcols)=6 for both; cell width for cells = pitch for all except maybe cells in left drawn with width = pitch-1 because there's a space reserved *after each meter except those in last overall column*? Left column's *aggregate meter* width passed as 47 but its internal MultiMeter drawing might pass each submeter a width = (47+1)/8=6 and start x increments 6, submeter draws in width6 but CPUMeter's bar mode decides to leave a trailing space if it is not the final submeter in the row? It could be that CPUMeters are joined with an extra blank x offset between aggregates? Wait each CPUMeter item as a Meter object has a `Meter_draw` that draws caption+bar, then MultiMeter advances by meter width +1. Meter width for each submeter = (totalWidth / subcols) -1 (separation) = 47/8=5 (floor 5) -? For right 48/8=6 -1=5 also.
        Something dimensions for right column must actually be 55 or 56 if its subcells drawn width6+pitch6. Could right column x be 44, not 50, with first right cell " 48[0]" starting at 50 because there's a left column trailing plus a *global header offset* of ??? Let's collect geometry at many terminal widths for CPUS8 to solve formulas later. Delay.
      */
      int subWidth = width / subcols;
      int pitch = subWidth;
      if(subWidth<1) subWidth=1;
      /* If there is remainder, distribute as 1-space separators between subcolumns to match W100 left case: remainder = width - subWidth*subcols; if remainder == subcols-1 (47 case subWidth5 rem7) pitch=subWidth+1 */
      int rem = width - subWidth*subcols;
      if(rem==subcols-1) pitch=subWidth+1;
      for(int r=0;r<rows;r++){
         for(int c=0;c<subcols;c++){
            int idx=c*rows+r;
            if(idx>=count) continue;
            int cpu=start+idx;
            int cx=x+c*pitch;
            int cw=subWidth;
            if(cx+cw>x+width) cw=x+width-cx;
            if(mode==2){
               /* Text mode multi CPU: each submeter text? Draw CPU text line truncated */
